==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*pо-}}. See {{m|ru|по|t=up to}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{ru-IPA|по́-}} {{i|when stressed}}

===Prefix===
{{head|ru|prefix|head=по-|head2=по́-|cat2=verbal prefixes}}

# [[perfective aspect]]
#: {{prefex|ru|-йти́|g1=impf|t1=to go|пойти́|g2=pf|t2=to go}}
# {{lb|ru|rare}} [[imperfective aspect]]
#: {{prefex|ru|купи́ть|g1=pf|t1=to buy, purchase|-а́ть|покупа́ть|g3=impf|t3=to buy, purchase}}
# for a [[while]], [[a little]] {{gloss|see [[w:delimitative aspect|delimitative aspect]]}}
#: {{prefex|ru|говори́ть|g1=impf|t1=to talk|поговори́ть|g2=pf|t2=to talk a bit, to chat}}
#: {{prefex|ru|рабо́тать|t1=to work|порабо́тать|t2=to work a bit}}
#: {{prefex|ru|спа́ть|t1= to sleep|поспа́ть|t2=to sleep a bit}}
# {{n-g|Added with a hyphen to certain adjectives to create adverbs, often (but not always) with the meaning "in the manner of behaviour, speech etc. of [the adjective]". Typically changes the adjective ending to the dative masculine/neuter singular ending, but the following additional changes also occur: {{m|ru|-ский}} to {{m|ru|-ски}}, {{m|ru|-ско́й}} to {{m|ru|-ски́}}, {{m|ru|-ий}} to {{m|ru|-ьи}}.}}
#: {{prefex|ru|ру́сский|t1=Russian|по-ру́сски|t2=in a Russian way, Russian (the language)}}
#: {{prefex|ru|мужско́й|t1=male, masculine|по-мужски́|t2=in a manly way, like a man}}
#: {{prefex|ru|ра́зный|t1=different, various|по-ра́зному|t2=in various ways, it depends}}
#: {{prefex|ru|дома́шний|t1=domestic, home|по-дома́шнему|t2=like at home}}
# place names
#: {{prefex|ru|Во́лга|t1=the [[Volga]] River|-ье|Пово́лжье|t3=[[Volga]] Region}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[поволжский|пово́лжские]] [[немец|не́мцы]]|[[Volga]] [[Germans]]}}
#: {{prefex|ru|Ла́ба|t1=the [[Elbe]] River|-ский|доли́на|t3=[[basin]]|Пола́бская доли́на|t4=[[Elbe]] River Basin}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[полабский|пола́бские]] [[славянин|славя́не]]|[[Polabian]] [[Slavs]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[Померания]]|[[Pomerania]]}}

====Usage notes====
* The stressed variant is found in the following situations:
*# the past participle of verbs with a one-syllable root ending in {{lang|ru|-ать}}, {{lang|ru|-нуть}} and some others: e.g. {{m|ru|по́жранный}} from {{m|ru|пожра́ть||to [[devour]]}}, {{m|ru|по́гнанный}} from {{m|ru|погна́ть||to [[drive]]}}, {{m|ru|по́гнутый}} from {{m|ru|погну́ть||to [[bend]]}}, {{m|ru|по́литый}}/{{m|ru|поли́тый}} from {{m|ru|поли́ть||to [[pour]], to [[water]]}};
*# the past tense of some verbs with a one-syllable root: e.g. {{m|ru|[[по́лил]], [[поли́л]]|pos=masculine singular past tense}} from {{m|ru|поли́ть||to [[pour]], to [[water]]}}, {{m|ru|по́мер|pos=masculine singular past tense}} from {{m|ru|помере́ть||to [[die]] {{i|colloquial}}}}, {{m|ru|[[по́дал]], [[пода́л]]|pos=masculine singular past tense}} from {{m|ru|пода́ть||to [[give]], to [[serve]] (food), to [[deliver]] (a [[vehicle]])}};
*# some deverbal nouns: e.g. {{m|ru|по́вод||[[cause]], [[reason]]}} from {{m|ru|води́ть||to [[lead]]}}, {{m|ru|по́греб||[[cellar]]}} from {{m|ru|погрести́||to [[bury]], to [[inter]]}}, {{m|ru|по́езд||[[train]]}} from {{m|ru|е́здить||to [[ride]], to [[drive]]}};
*# some adverbs: e.g. {{m|ru|по́верху||on [[top]], on the [[surface]] {{i|colloquial}}}}, {{m|ru|по́пусту||to [[no]] [[purpose]], for [[nothing]] {{i|colloquial}}}}.

